{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.TwoRowDimCatalan","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mathlib.TwoRowDimCatalan","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.BallotNumbers","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.SYTBranching2Row"],"declarations":9,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.corank_value_eight","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.corank_value_eight","kind":"theorem","line":169,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/TwoRowDimCatalan.lean#L169-L170","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.corank_value_seven","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.corank_value_seven","kind":"theorem","line":166,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/TwoRowDimCatalan.lean#L166-L167","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.corank_value_six","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.corank_value_six","kind":"theorem","line":163,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/TwoRowDimCatalan.lean#L163-L164","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.corank_value_five","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.corank_value_five","kind":"theorem","line":160,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/TwoRowDimCatalan.lean#L160-L161","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.corank_value_four","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.corank_value_four","kind":"theorem","line":157,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/TwoRowDimCatalan.lean#L157-L158","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.corank_value_three","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.corank_value_three","kind":"theorem","line":154,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/TwoRowDimCatalan.lean#L154-L155","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.factorial_sub_two_row_sq_sum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.factorial_sub_two_row_sq_sum","kind":"theorem","line":134,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/TwoRowDimCatalan.lean#L134-L144","doc":"**The general-`n` rank accounting**: `n!` minus the visible-block dimension\ncount is `n! − catalan n`.\n\nThis is the arithmetic identity that `QOU.QBeta.MarkovGramDegenerate.corank_three`\n/ `_four` / `_five` were three hand-computed instances of. Those wrote the\ntwo-row dimensions out by hand (`1, 2` / `1, 3, 2` / `1, 4, 5`); this derives\nthe whole count from `catalan n` with nothing listed by hand. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.dimHLF_two_row_sq_sum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.dimHLF_two_row_sq_sum","kind":"theorem","line":114,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/TwoRowDimCatalan.lean#L114-L132","doc":"**`Σ_{k ≤ ⌊n/2⌋} (dim S^{(n−k,k)})² = catalan n`.**\n\nThe sum of squared dimensions over all partitions of `n` with at most two rows\nis the `n`-th Catalan number — for every `n`, with the dimensions given by the\nFrame–Robinson–Thrall hook length formula rather than by a closed form assumed\nin advance.\n\nEquivalently, by RSK, 321-avoiding permutations of `n` are counted by `C_n`;\nbut the proof goes nowhere near RSK — see `BallotNumbers.ballot_sq_sum_catalan`\nfor the reflection-plus-Vandermonde argument that replaces it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.dimHLF_two_row_eq_ballot","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.dimHLF_two_row_eq_ballot","kind":"theorem","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/TwoRowDimCatalan.lean#L83-L112","doc":"**The two-row hook-length dimension is the ballot number**, in `ballot`'s\nindexing: `dim S^{(n−k,k)} = m_k(n)` whenever `2k ≤ n`.\n\n`dimHLF_pair` already says this as a `ℕ` difference of binomials; the work here\nis the cast to `ℤ`, which needs `C(n,k−1) ≤ C(n,k)` so that the truncated `ℕ`\nsubtraction agrees with the honest `ℤ` one. That monotonicity holds precisely\nbelow the centre of the row, i.e. exactly under the hypothesis `2k ≤ n` that\nmakes `(n−k, k)` a partition — so the side condition is not an artefact, it is\nthe same condition twice.\n\nThe `k = 0` case is separate because `m_0` is pinned rather than computed\n(see `ballot`); there the shape is `(n)` with an empty second row and\n`dimHLF_zero_row` gives `1`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}